  "derivation": "p1 seq=1000 len=100 establishes the high-water mark at 1100 (never a retransmission). p2 seq=1100 len=100 advances it to 1200. p3 seq=1100 len=100 ends at 1200 <= 1200 -> RETRANSMISSION (100 bytes). p4 seq=1000 len=100 ends at 1100 <= 1200 -> RETRANSMISSION (100 bytes). p5 and p6 are zero-length pure ACKs with an identical sequence number: eff_len = 0, so they are NOT seq-bearing and NOT retransmissions \u2014 this is the duplicate-ACK exclusion. p7 seq=1200 len=50 ends at 1250 > 1200 -> new data. retrans = 2, retrans bytes = 200, seq-bearing = 5 (p1,p2,p3,p4,p7), ratio = 2/5.",
